{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/158451-the-dreaming","id":158451,"title":"The Dreaming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-03T17:49:53-07:00","id":158451,"title":"The Dreaming","content":"Okay, I'm starting this with kid gloves on, because the thread that I began for North America (see The Spirit Nation thread) first had some interesting thoughts, but then devolved into god exclusion and some people considering making a Native American pantheon &quot;racist&quot;, and then it meandered into the Abrahamic Pantheon thread for a bit. *ugh*<br /> <br /> I tried to make something of the untapped potential of North America and Australia, mainly for the reason that I don't want these two places in 2E Scion to be seen merely as land grabs for the other pantheons out there. (For North America, my fear extends to the thought that the Aztec pantheon would absorb the Southwestern tribes into their mindset, The Aesir, Pesdajet, Tuatha, and Dodekethon would fight over the Eastern and Midwestern reservations for worshippers, the Loa would take the swamp people of the Southeast. and the Amatsukami and the Chinese Bureaucracy would squabble over those left on the West Coast and Pacific Northwest.) (For Australia, the battle would be between the Orisha, Chinese Bureacracy and the Amatsukami). <br /> <br /> This is NOT what I want to see happen in these areas in 2E Scion. That's why I started to try to make The Spirit Nation to honor the culture of the Native Americans in a game of Modern Myths and Urban Fantasy.<br /> <br /> So anyway, for Australia I was thinking of something that revolved around the Aboriginal system of The Dreaming. Can anyone help me with this, because I know of only three things:<br /> <br /> 1. Thanks to a trivia question that I saw riding home once, the Aboriginals believed that the Koala was responsible for the rains that occur in Australia.<br /> <br /> 2. This pantheon would SO be masters of the Illusion purview.<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> 3. I could see the walkabout being the first Visitation for Australian Scions.<br /> <br /> So what is the Dreaming and how can it be formed into a pantheon for Australia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T18:23:50-07:00","id":158504,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;Dreamtime&quot; is where all times exists, and where the soul/spirit goes before it passes on to reincarnate (?) &quot;Dreaming&quot; is what your reality is now, your beliefs and all that makes you &quot;you&quot; as well as what your tribe's laws and ethics are. I'm sure someone else has a better idea than my half-assed phrasing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T21:10:59-07:00","id":158677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/158451-the-dreaming#post158451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I'm starting this with kid gloves on, because the thread that I began for North America (see The Spirit Nation thread) first had some interesting thoughts, but then devolved into god exclusion and some people considering making a Native American pantheon &quot;racist&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear, what was objected to is saying that all Native Americans are the same and don't deserve the same cultural attention or diversity as Europeans, Africans and Asians. The same thing applies to the Australian Aboriginal people. They're more than one group. They do have some things in common, but the people inland work differently from the coastal dwellers, and so forth.<br /> <br /> Again, this is a time to really dive in and research the subject material, find one or two cultures that have enough material on them (and the Australian Aboriginal cultures have survived, even increased in numbers since colonization, so resources do exist, and they're even available in English sometimes!) to create a distinct Pantheon. If you want examples of two different Aboriginal groups, there's the northern coastal Murrinh-Patha people or the centrally-located Pintupi people.<br /> <br /> I am <i>not</i> saying that Australia doesn't deserve a Pantheon to represent it. I think that having a Pantheon from North America and Australia is an <i><b>absolutely awesome idea</b></i> and something that Scion really needs to do. But, it should be done as respectfully and carefully as possible, just as if it was being done for one of the three Old World continents. What I think would be <i>even more awesome</i> is having an African, North American, South American and Oceanic/Australian Pantheon. Basically cover all the globe so each major region gets at least one representative. There's a huge selection to pick from! Literally thousands! And, technically, North America <i>has</i> a Pantheon: the Aztecs. They're from North America, not South America. However a lot of folks in the US tend to lump everything below Texas into &quot;South America&quot; despite what geography and the people living there have to say. So for their sake, and the Loas', we'll say they're Central American.<br /> <br /> Currently what Scion offers is in <b>bold</b>and potential recruits are listed in <i>italics</i>.<br /> <br /> Central America: <b>Aztecs, Loa</b><br /> Europe: <b>Greeks, Norse, Irish</b><br /> The Middle East: <b>Egyptians, Yazatas</b><br /> Asia: <b>Chinese, Japanese, Hindu</b><br /> <br /> North America: None <i>(potentials: Navajo, Cherokee, Inuit, Lakota, etc)</i><br /> South America: None<i> (potentials: Inca, Guarani)</i><br /> Sub-Saharan Africa: None <i>(potentials: Yoruba, Masai, Bantu, Zulu, etc)</i><br /> Australia/Oceania: None <i>(potentials: Maori, Pintupi, Murrinh-Patha)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":235,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","user":"Telgar","date":".  EDIT: whups, totally forgot the Hindu Pantheon. 06-04-2014, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T22:16:32-07:00","id":159753,"title":"","content":"Understood. I'm glad that this new edition will be open-ended, which hopefully also means OGL, so everything can have a proper inclusion to the world that is Scion. Also, what are the other belief systems of the Aboriginies? I'm asking because the Dreamtime and Dreaming seemed to be the most prevalent when looking at books and movies based on Australia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T22:30:44-07:00","id":159765,"title":"","content":"Dreamtime and Dreaming aren't a religion. They're elements that appear frequently in Australia and the surrounding areas. If you want to learn more about the religions of the different Australian Aboriginal cultures, you'd have to do some research.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T09:28:07-07:00","id":160024,"title":"","content":"One reason the concept shows up a lot because it was a part of the navigation system to get people across the desert. Landmarks and routes from landmark (including some astronomy as well) to were associated with particular myths. Resources were very scarce. Horribly scarce. Getting from place to place was a matter of life and death. So different tribes/bands/cultures/language groups would share the same PRECISE myth/story/songline/road map. You get it wrong, you get lost in trackless waste and die. So some stories get repeated again and again or span wide ranges of peoples/areas. It doesn't make everyone who shares the same stories the same people and some of their stories (particularly the ones tied up in their particular initiation rites) would be VERY different, even if other stories were shared. Even involving the same divine beings.<br /> <br /> So.... it's complicated. And a lot of the resources are, not surprisingly, Australian and haven't made their way onto the net. I got a lot of what I know from an anthropology professor who did most of his fieldwork in the Outback. I've also managed to pick up some good sources in secondhand bookstores over the years. But it's been hit and miss and largely a matter of luck. I don't know that I have enough to feel confident to put together a decent pantheon. I've just used the material to provide an interesting one-off figure for a particular purpose. (Like having an Australian mythical figure pop up for an adventure... like having a summit of Pacific Rim deities called by the Amatsukami concerned with the manifestations of Tawhirimatea and the possibility of him spawning typoons that would destroy their associated mortal followers, followed by the BIGGEST of the BIG ones when he comes through. Also used a mythical being, the Wugaru, to create another race of Prometheans.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T09:31:16-07:00","id":160028,"title":"","content":"Also, incidentally, a very similar thing is going on with the Polynesian diaspora. A lot of myths are shared because they were an important part of the navigation system from island to island. So there are lots of different areas with different myths/mythic figures but there is also a lot of connection and repetition. It's hard with the Polynesians to draw a line about where one pantheon would begin and another end. Though, when you look at the big view, there is arguably a lot more difference between the myths of the Maori in New Zealand and those of the Hawaiians then there are between those of the Irish and the Welsh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}